# https://w3id.org/spot#Appearance
<https://w3id.org/spot#Appearance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Appearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The appearance of an entity space in a reference space (Asset, Document or another Entity Space).\r\n    The appearance object serves as a container/reference to assign spatial relation definitions for the relationship\r\n    between the Entity Space instance and the space where it appears in."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Appearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Appearance"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace
<https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#EntitySpace> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A two-dimensional space that can be used to represent resources like 2D drawings or maps "@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Area Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#AssetAppearance
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#Appearance> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The appearance of entity space in an asset space"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Asset Appearance"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#AssetSpace
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#PhysicalSpace> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\"The Asset Space represents the actual, physical asset.\r\n        An instance of the Asset Space is the superordinate object for the spatial superimposition of Entity Space instances."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#AssetSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Asset Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#Axis
<https://w3id.org/spot#Axis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Axis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An axis of the local coordinate system of a space instance"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Axis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Axis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#Direction
<https://w3id.org/spot#Direction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Direction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The defined direction of an axis (e.g., an X-Axis is pointing to the 'Front' of the asset,\r\n     or an Y-Axis is pointing to the 'Bottom' of a document / plan ).\r\n     Only Asset Space or Document Space Axis should get an Direction Definition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Direction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Direction"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentAppearance
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#Appearance> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The appearance of an entity space in a document space"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentAppearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document Appearance"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentSpace
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#VirtualSpace> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Document Space represents the extent of a document or file that contains Entity Spaces.\r\n    A Document Space can represent different, disjointed Entity Spaces, such as a collection of sections and\r\n     details on a construction plan."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#DocumentSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document Space"@en .
