<https://w3id.org/spot#EntitySpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#PhysicalSpace> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#EntitySpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Entity Space is a coherent unit of information covered by a single resource, such as a 3D model,\r\n     a 2D drawing, or a picture, representing its actual dimensions referring to the Asset Space."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#EntitySpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entity Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#HorizontalAreaSpace
<https://w3id.org/spot#HorizontalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#HorizontalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#HorizontalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Horizontal Area Space is a subtype of Area Space, that implies that the plane of the resource\r\n     is parallel to the horizontal plane of the asset space. Floorplans or maps are typical horizontal area spaces."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#HorizontalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Horizontal Area Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#LineSpace
