<https://w3id.org/spot#PointSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Point Space can represent resources that only need one point of reference,\r\n    such as the camera position of a picture or the position of a sensor."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#PointSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Point Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#Space
<https://w3id.org/spot#Space> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Space> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The abstract superclass for all defined space types."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#Space> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#VerticalAreaSpace
<https://w3id.org/spot#VerticalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#VerticalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#AreaSpace> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#VerticalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Vertical Area Space is a subtype of Area Space, that implies that the plane of the resource is\r\n     parallel to the vertical axis of the asset space. Section drawings are typical vertical area spaces."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#VerticalAreaSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vertical Area Space"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot#VirtualSpace
<https://w3id.org/spot#VirtualSpace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#VirtualSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot#Space> .
<https://w3id.org/spot#VirtualSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Virtual Space represent resource spaces, which cannot be directly mapped to the real physical space,\r\n     as their spatial arrangement is artificial. For example 2D plans with a collection of drawings\r\n     or a file containing multiple disjointed 3D models of the same asset.  It is an abstract class and should not be used directly."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot#VirtualSpace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Virtual Space"@en .
